  {
    "id": "72db4692bae0",
    "text": "The saddest thing a child can believe\nis that love comes with conditions —\nthat they're only loved when they're easy.\nSo when they mess up,\nthey don't just feel guilty.\nThey feel the distance widen between us.\nThat's the quiet cost of discipline without warmth.\nThe limit stays — and so do you.\nThat's why repair matters more than the rule.\nBecause held after falling, love never left.",
